        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a6d49f1b-f6d4-552a-abc5-02d61afc2cd8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Thompson, Theodore H. White, David L. Wolper, John Curran, Paige Curran\n- Works: Savage Night, China: The Roots of Madness\n- Roles: author, screenwriter, political journalist, historian, producer\n- Topics: hardboiled crime fiction, wartime reporting from China, U.S. presidential elections, Cold War television documentaries\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Thompson was born on September 27, 1906, and he was an American author and screenwriter known for hardboiled crime fiction.\n- Theodore H. White was born on May 6, 1915, and he was an American political journalist and historian known for wartime reporting from China and for accounts of the 1960, 1964, 1968, 1972, 1976, and 1980 presidential elections.\n- Savage Night is a 1953 novel by thriller writer Jim Thompson.\n- China: The Roots of Madness is a 1967 Cold War-era made-for-TV documentary film produced by David L. Wolper and written by Theodore H. White.\n- The production cost of China: The Roots of Madness was funded by a donation from John Curran and Paige Curran.\n- Jim Thompson died on April 7, 1977.\n- Theodore H. White died on May 15, 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
